Humming executes 13.88% fewer instructions (custom executes 16.12% more) and
4.70x fewer branch instructions despite its scheduler loop.  High occupancy is
not the differentiator.  The evidence favors a one-warpgroup persistent W2
that initializes mbarriers/LUT once, advances barrier phase across tasks, and
uses enough packed-weight stages to cover all four K128 tiles.  It disfavors
the rejected second producer warpgroup.

For context, the same current Humming capture measured W13 at 137.152 us,
42,861,628 instructions, grid 234, 124 registers/thread and 53.248 KiB/CTA.
The accepted custom historical detailed report measured W13 at 138.144 us,
so W13 remains effectively tied and is outside the next candidate's scope.

